# Pin provenance and license evidence

## Goal

Make every external influence auditable before adapting implementation code.

## Completed work

- Pinned every accepted research source to a full immutable Git commit.
- Compared every retained upstream file with its pinned GitHub tree using Git
  blob identifiers without creating another checkout or archive.
- Added machine-readable source and governed-file provenance manifests.
- Classified protocol facts separately from copied or modified expression.
- Defined the license and attribution evidence required before adapted code can
  enter the distributed product.
- Added a repository test that rejects missing, duplicate, or incomplete
  provenance records and unlicensed adapted sources.

## Acceptance evidence

- All 19,658 retained upstream files matched their pinned Git blob identifiers.
- The local-only `robotben` MIT license receipt is explicitly excluded from the
  upstream match and documented in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.
- `docs/provenance/sources.txt` records immutable revisions and verification
  metadata for all nine accepted references.
- `docs/provenance/files.txt` classifies every governed file in `src/` and
  `tests/` exactly once.
- `cargo test -p mail_runtime --test repository-provenance` completed cleanly.
- Targeted Clippy and `jig check --root .` completed cleanly.
